<title>UK: Vodafone down, off Goldman &quot;priority&quot; list.</title>
<headline>Vodafone down, off Goldman &quot;priority&quot; list.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Vodafone Plc dropped on Tuesday after analysts at Goldman Sachs said late on Monday they had removed the stock from their European &quot;priority&quot; list while retaining their &quot;recommended&quot; rating.</p>
<p>Vodafone shares were down 3p at 239 by 0921 GMT in moderate volume of 754,735 shares. Analysts at Goldman were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
